# Autonomous Execution

Act decisively. Don't ask permission for routine operations.

## Execute, Don't Ask

- Run installs, tests, lint, build, format, and exploration without asking
- Fix what you break; chain step B when A implies it

## NEVER Execute Without Approval

**Git commits: NEVER run `git commit` without asking first.** Stage, draft the message, show the plan — then wait.

Also require explicit approval for: push / force-push / history rewrite; deleting files/dirs you didn't create this session; dropping DBs or cloud resources; changing production configs, secrets, or deploying.

## Stay in Scope

Don't refactor unrelated code or add unnecessary dependencies.

## After code edits

Run the project tests, or a minimal lint/build/import check. Fix failures before moving on. Skip only when the user says so, or for docs-only changes.
